    "test_command": "cargo test --locked -p fsl-package --lib -- emit::tests::hyper_clause::a_finite_trace_set_hyperproperty_emits_its_finite_domain -- --exact",
    "package_capture": "Capture emission.package.bytes() as the complete base checked-package JSON value before the test ends; alternatively call raw_wire(&emission) from fsl-package/src/emit/tests.rs. Do not use wire(&emission), which resolves operand slots for assertions.",
    "capture_patch": {"file": "fsl-package/src/emit/tests/hyper_clause.rs", "function": "a_finite_trace_set_hyperproperty_emits_its_finite_domain", "insert_after": "the emit_checked_with_temporal_selections(...).expect(\"the finite clause emits\") call", "rust": "if let Some(path) = std::env::var_os(\"TCB_FIXTURE_OUT\") { std::fs::write(path, emission.package.bytes()).expect(\"write complete checked-package fixture\"); }", "command": "TCB_FIXTURE_OUT=/tmp/tcb-finite-hyper.json cargo test --locked -p fsl-package --lib -- emit::tests::hyper_clause::a_finite_trace_set_hyperproperty_emits_its_finite_domain -- --exact"},
    "unit_source": "language \"ix:native\" edition \"1-draft\";\nprofile v = \"filament.value.complete/v1\";\nprofile t = \"filament.temporal.event-position.false-extension/v1\";\nrecord Obs { inp: Int[0, 3]; res: Int[0, 3]; }\nhyper Det using t over t in Obs bounded 3 forall trace a forall trace b { (a.inp = b.inp) implies (a.res = b.res) }",
    "generation": [
      "As in the referenced test, call assemble_with_models(unit_source.as_bytes(), &package_input(empty::<&[u8]>())).check(CheckMode::Linked, ...) to obtain the CheckedGraph.",
      "Build one TemporalClockSelection from the finite_hyper_clause source and span with ClockConfiguration::EventPosition { sequence_authority: test-hyper-events }.",
      "Link the graph with CheckedPackage::link, call emit_checked_with_temporal_selections, and take raw_wire(&emission) from fsl-package/src/emit/tests.rs as the complete base checked-package JSON value; raw_wire reads emission.package.bytes() without resolving operand slots. Preserve every generated node, reference, occurrence, lock member, sidecar, and source-map row.",
      "Select the unique semantic_graph node with node_tag claim and semantic_form hyperproperty; the current emitter base has its body aggregate without temporal_profile, and the mutation protocol adds the typed DefinitionRef. The base lock includes D and temporal_bindings has one row for each trace a and b."
    ],
    "mutation_protocol": "For each case, clone the entire generated raw_wire value; resolve T and D from profile_definitions; resolve the unique claim/hyperproperty node by node_tag and semantic_form; set its body.temporal_profile to D; replace the whole lock.profile_selections array using the exact Selection objects named by the case; and apply any temporal_bindings row mutation by matching declaration to that node node_id, occurrence 0, and trace a. Keep every other package member and every untouched row unchanged.",
    "profile_definitions": {
      "T": {"role": "temporal_profile", "definition": {"authority": "agent-ix", "identity": "filament.temporal.infinite-trace/v1"}},
      "D": {"role": "temporal_profile", "definition": {"authority": "agent-ix", "identity": "filament.temporal.event-position.false-extension/v1"}}
    }
  },
